1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
In the CLO, use the template to build the model.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Like these three small cube.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Take it out as OPT.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Then put this OPT into the name line to use.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Be careful before you export.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Put the model in place first.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
It is placed in the middle like this now.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Put it on the floor and check it in the 3D window.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Does it show the floor grid?

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Find the X-axis according to the floor grid.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The name line will repeat along the X-axis.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Refer to this picture.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
This is the direction of the three axes in the 3D window.

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Go back to the software.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Press the shortcut 5 to switch to the 5-angle.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
In the case of the 5-angle, the X-axis is horizontal.

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The name line will follow the blue, red, and yellow.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Press the shortcut 5 to switch to the 5-angle.

19
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Then export it to OPT.

20
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
In the menu bar, export, OPT.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Select an address.

22
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Save it to the desktop first.

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Remember the name.

24
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
This is the export OPT window.

25
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Let's take a look at the information in here.

26
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
You can watch this video about the settings of the export OPT.

27
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
I won't talk about all the options in here.

28
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Let's set it directly.

29
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Set a single target.

30
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The thick one.

31
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Click on the unified UV coordinates.

32
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
As long as the slow shooting picture is OK.

33
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The發現 picture is not needed.

34
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Then go down.

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Save it with the text file.

36
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Just save it as a compressed package.

37
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Click OK.

38
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
The compressed package after export is on the desktop.

39
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Right-click to unzip.

40
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Open the file after unzipping.

41
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
You can see the corresponding OPT file.

42
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Go back to the software.

43
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Open the file of this skirt.

44
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Next, complete the strap of this skirt.

45
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Switch to the thick texture surface.

46
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Turn off the display of the inner line and the basic line.

47
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Zoom in to see the model shoulder.

48
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Create a new name line.

49
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Click add.

50
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The OPT name line window will appear.

51
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
The left side is the corresponding setting.

52
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The right side is the preview window.

53
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
It's still empty at this time.

54
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
You need to add the OPT file first.

55
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
See here.

56
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,000
There is a browse button.

57
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Click the browse button.

58
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Open the OPT file just exported.

59
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
The length and width of the display is the size of the OPT file.

60
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
And it appears in the preview window.

61
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
At this time, its scale is 0.

62
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:20,000
The scale refers to the distance between each OPT unit.

63
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
When exporting before.

64
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Three small objects are exported together.

65
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Then they are a unit.

66
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
After modifying the scale to 10mm.

67
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
The distance between three small objects and the next group of small objects.

68
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Changed to 10mm.

69
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
The scale is changed to 0.

70
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
See this part above.

71
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Here you can modify the ratio.

72
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
The rotation of the axis can make the OPT.

73
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Rotate on the axis of X, Y, and Z.

74
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Here you don't need to select.

75
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Because we have already set it at the beginning.

76
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Now just import it directly.

77
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Modify the settings.

78
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
The scale refers to the number of lines we have added.

79
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
The distance between the inner line and the outer line of the board.

80
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Changed to 0.

81
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Use the free line tool.

82
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Add the number of lines to the board.

83
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The number of lines added is gray.

84
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Because the corresponding UV image has not been added yet.

85
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Select the number of lines at the object window.

86
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Then click the browse button at the back of the text.

87
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Add the UV image.

88
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
The rest of the shoulder boards are also added to the number of lines.

89
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Finally, hide the bottom sheet.

90
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Click the fabric used for the shoulder board.

91
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Change the opacity of the fabric to 0.

92
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:07,000
The surface is now clean.

93
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
The surface of the fabric is now clean.

94
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
The surface of the board is now clean.

95
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
The surface of the board is now clean.

96
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
The surface of the board is now clean.

